      "side": 1,
      "message": "This approach is a bit risky as it could delete backup files generated by other means. \n\nThe issue seems to be that BSD sed need a backup extension specified, and that extension can be null (if separated by a space from the -i). We can detect the BSD sed (some people may have GNU sed on MacOs) by assuming it does not support the --version switch and testing for that (a better test would be great, but I haven\u0027t found one). With that in mind, this should work:\n\n```\nSPACE_FOR_BSD_SED\u003d$(sed --version \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 || echo -n \u0027 \u0027)\nfind . -name \"*.java\" | xargs sed -i$SPACE_FOR_BSD_SED\u0027\u0027 s/jakarta.servlet/javax.servlet/\n```",
      "revId": "24517050a7fec935277e853ff1d3e041d4b9144d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
